ph:China_Ad5_Ebola_Vaccine a idmp:MedicinalProduct ;
    ph:medicalCountermeasureType "vaccine"@en ;
    ph:sourcePage 51 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 51] In 2017, the Chinese National Medical Products Administration (NMPA) approved the application for registration of a recombinant Ebola virus vaccine based on adenovirus technology. The vaccine was developed and produced in China. It uses a recombinant adenovirus type 5 (Ad5) vector, which has been engineered to carry the gene for the glycoprotein (GP) of the Ebola virus, prompting an immune response to protect against Ebola virus infection."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Recombinant adenovirus type 5 Ebola vaccine"@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasTherapeuticIndication ph:China_Ad5_Ebola_Vaccine_Ebola_Virus_Disease_PREVENTION_Indication .

ph:China_Bivalent_Hantavirus_Vaccine a idmp:MedicinalProduct ;
    ph:medicalCountermeasureType "vaccine"@en ;
    ph:sourcePage 71 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 71] China has approved both monovalent and bivalent inactivated vaccines that target the Hantaan and Seoul viruses. These are included in national immunisation programmes in endemic areas and have contributed to a marked decrease in HFRS cases."@en ;
