ph:Sabin_Marburg_Vaccine a idmp:MedicinalProduct ;
    ph:medicalCountermeasureType "vaccine"@en ;
    ph:sourcePage 51 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 51] There are currently no licensed vaccines for MVD, but several promising candidates are in various stages of development. The Sabin Vaccine Institute has launched a Phase 2 clinical trial of its Marburg virus vaccine in Kenya and Uganda. The University of Oxford has initiated a first-in-was also used in the recent Marburg virus disease outbreak in Rwanda, despite not having been included in the planned clinical trials."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sabin Marburg virus vaccine candidate"@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasTherapeuticIndication ph:Sabin_Marburg_Vaccine_Marburg_Virus_Disease_PREVENTION_Indication .

ph:Sabin_Sudan_Ebola_Vaccine a idmp:MedicinalProduct ;
    ph:medicalCountermeasureType "vaccine"@en ;
    ph:sourcePage 51 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 51] There are currently no licensed vaccines for Sudan ebolavirus, but several candidates are under development. In particular, the Sabin Vaccine Institute has initiated Phase 2 clinical trials for its Sudan ebolavirus vaccine in Kenya and Uganda. The International AIDS Vaccine Initiative (IAVI) is (in partnership with Merck and supported by CEPI and BARDA) developing a Sudan virus vaccine candidate (IAVI SUDV-GP), which is based on the VSV platform that is also used in the licensed Zaire ebolavirus vaccine (Ervebo). The US FDA has granted orphan d and post-exposure prophylaxis against Sudan ebolavirus infection."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sabin Sudan ebolavirus vaccine candidate"@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasTherapeuticIndication ph:Sabin_Sudan_Ebola_Vaccine_Sudan_Virus_Disease_PREVENTION_Indication .

