ph:Dectova_Avian_Influenza_TREATMENT_Indication a idmp:TherapeuticIndication ;
    ph:sourcePage 39,
        40 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 39] Seasonal prevention with oseltamivir may be considered for individuals aged one year or older. The approved labels for influenza antivirals include recommendations for the use of PrEP in exceptional circumstances (for example, if there is a mismatch between circulating and vaccine virus strains) and in a pandemic situation. It can therefore be considered in escalating scenarios where there are human cases in the EU/EEA especially if there are clusters of cases according to national recommendations for specific groups (e.g. workers involved in culling infected animals), household contacts of confirmed human cases or healthcare workers. It should be noted that prolonged use may have implications for safety or resistance emergence."@en,
        "[p. 40] Dectova, GSK Zanamivir (intravenous)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Zoonotic influenza is generally susceptible to seasonal-influenza antivirals; use should follow national and WHO guidance."@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasIndicationAsDiseaseSymptomProcedure ph:Avianflu ;
    idmp:isApplicableIn cmns-ge-euj:EuropeanUnion .

ph:Dectova_Seasonal_Influenza_TREATMENT_Indication a idmp:TherapeuticIndication ;
    ph:sourcePage 39,
        40 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 39] Seasonal prevention with oseltamivir may be considered for individuals aged one year or older. The approved labels for influenza antivirals include recommendations for the use of PrEP in exceptional circumstances (for example, if there is a mismatch between circulating and vaccine virus strains) and in a pandemic situation. It can therefore be considered in escalating scenarios where there are human cases in the EU/EEA especially if there are clusters of cases according to national recommendations for specific groups (e.g. workers involved in culling infected animals), household contacts of confirmed human cases or healthcare workers. It should be noted that prolonged use may have implications for safety or resistance emergence."@en,
        "[p. 40] Dectova, GSK Zanamivir (intravenous)"@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasIndicationAsDiseaseSymptomProcedure ph:Seasonal_Influenza ;
    idmp:isApplicableIn cmns-ge-euj:EuropeanUnion .

