ph:Veklury_Nipah_Virus_Disease_TREATMENT_Indication a idmp:TherapeuticIndication ;
    ph:sourcePage 59 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 59] There are currently no approved antiviral treatments for Hendra or Nipah virus infections in humans. Treatment is primarily supportive and often involves measures to manage symptoms such as fever, respiratory distress and neurological complications."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Remdesivir showed efficacy in non-human primate models when administered soon after infection; human evidence remains very limited."@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasIndicationAsDiseaseSymptomProcedure ph:Nipah_Virus_Disease ;
    idmp:isApplicableIn ph:Global .

ph:Veklury_Sudan_Virus_Disease_TREATMENT_Indication a idmp:TherapeuticIndication ;
    ph:sourcePage 52 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 52] There are no licensed therapeutics for Sudan ebolavirus, but several candidates are under development (most notably the monoclonal antibody MBP134 a cocktail of two broadly neutralising human monoclonal antibodies developed by the Sabin Vaccine Institute and partners, which has demonstrated protective efficacy in preclinical studies against both Ebola and Sudan viruses -specific mAb and investigational antivirals like remdesivir). Ongoing efforts are being Blueprint."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Remdesivir is mentioned as an investigational antiviral for Sudan virus disease."@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasIndicationAsDiseaseSymptomProcedure ph:Sudan_Virus_Disease ;
    idmp:isApplicableIn ph:Global .

