ph:Zabdeno_Ebola_Virus_Disease_PREVENTION_Indication a idmp:TherapeuticIndication ;
    ph:sourcePage 50,
        51 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 50] contains a virus known as Modified Vaccinia Ankara (MVA), which was engineered by Bavarian Nordic and has been modified to produce four proteins from Zaire ebolavirus and proteins from three other members of Filoviridae. It is part of a two-dose vaccine regimen and is administered in combination with Zabdeno (Ad26.ZEBOV-GP). The vaccine has demonstrated effectiveness in preventing EVD caused by the Zaire ebolavirus. o Zabdeno (Ad26.ZEBOV-GP [recombinant]; Janssen-Cilag International"@en,
        "[p. 51] expresses the glycoprotein of the Zaire ebolavirus Mayinga variant. It is a two-dose vaccine: Zabdeno is given as the first dose and Mvabea is given as the second dose eight weeks later. Zabdeno is effective in preventing EVD caused by the Zaire ebolavirus. The two-dose schedule, requiring an eight-week interval between doses, means that this combination vaccine would only be suitable for pre-exposure prophylaxis outside an outbreak situation."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Suitable for pre-exposure prophylaxis outside an outbreak situation because the second dose follows eight weeks later."@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasIndicationAsDiseaseSymptomProcedure ph:Ebola ;
    idmp:isApplicableIn cmns-ge-euj:EuropeanUnion .

ph:Zabdeno_Mvabea_Regimen_Ebola_Virus_Disease_PREVENTION_Indication a idmp:TherapeuticIndication ;
    ph:sourcePage 50,
        51 ;
    ph:sourceText "[p. 50] - Zabdeno and Mvabea heterologous regimen (Janssen-Cilag/Bavarian Nordic):"@en,
        "[p. 51] expresses the glycoprotein of the Zaire ebolavirus Mayinga variant. It is a two-dose vaccine: Zabdeno is given as the first dose and Mvabea is given as the second dose eight weeks later. Zabdeno is effective in preventing EVD caused by the Zaire ebolavirus. The two-dose schedule, requiring an eight-week interval between doses, means that this combination vaccine would only be suitable for pre-exposure prophylaxis outside an outbreak situation."@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom ph:HERA_Virus_Prioritisation_Report ;
    idmp:hasIndicationAsDiseaseSymptomProcedure ph:Ebola ;
    idmp:isApplicableIn cmns-ge-euj:EuropeanUnion .

